Z||000000||Denise||06-21-2000||10:06 PM||||OK.. yeah I know.. don't Razz me!! <P>I've been looking and looking... from what I can see Turbo's installations are mostly piping from and to the exh, and from and to the intake,  <BR>So.. I can buy a turbo,, found a source for stainless and alum tubing.  I'm sure piping is not my weakness, ( my dad was a plumber) welding I can get done.. <P>SC's.. as i see it the "front" of the Fiero 2.8 hasn't enough room for a SC blower like rotorex or paxton...  A shaft? put the blower near the bell housing or under the rear ex manifold?  <P>Thinking..<P>Denise, <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||06-21-2000||10:46 PM||||That's one way it's been done. <P>Look at the GM FWD performace page. There is a picture of the 3400 Supercharged proto engine (we'll never see it in production) using an Eaton M-45 or M-62. A long shaft runs back to the blower which is by the trans.<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
